Scorbutic swollen gums. Mouth feels cold;
putrid, impure breath. Pyorrhoea. [Merc, cor.; Causi.;
Staph.; Kreos.] Hurts to protrude the tongue.

Itching all over. Small, painful pisnples;
lupus. Glands inflamed and indurated. Mercurio-syph-
ilitic ulcers. Skin of hands hard, thick, dry, fissured ;
deep cracks. Itching of swollen hands and arms; gen-
eral itching which prevents sleep. Hemicrania.
